# Drafted by Gemini (R22 n1), edited.

~ fall_start
Narrator: For a breath, the foyer shines warm under a lit chandelier, until a body drops on a hemp rope and the whole house blows outward into spinning floorboards, a clawfoot bathtub, and a bewildered moose head.
cutscene nm_house_shatters
set nm_pit_started
if not quest.crooked_nightmare >= crooked_pit
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_pit
endif
crooked_man [smile]: Step right down, folks, mind the missing stairs! Old Eustace kept the parlor warm, and we are falling right on schedule!
cutscene nm_house_shatters_2
Narrator: The floor goes next, crumbling into a bottomless pit, and the attic boards hang far above through the wreckage.
cutscene nm_house_shatters_3
Narrator: Nobody says a word on the way down, which the Crooked Man takes for applause.
cutscene end
* Ask what he wants -> wants
* [Insight DC 14] Read him -> read_ok | read_fail
* [Performance DC 12] Laugh at him, loudly -> laugh_ok | laugh_fail
* Draw steel -> fight

~ wants
crooked_man [sly]: Just a full house again, neighbours, a proper Lockwood gathering with every name inked neat in the ledger! What is a manor without guests who never quite manage to leave?
-> fall_start_menu

~ fall_start_menu
crooked_man [smile]: Down we tumble through the lady's cellar of a mind, so tell me how you want to play it!
* [Insight DC 14] Read him -> read_ok | read_fail
* [Performance DC 12] Laugh at him, loudly -> laugh_ok | laugh_fail
* Draw steel -> fight

~ read_ok
Narrator: Behind his showman's leer, his milky eye twitches whenever one of you steps between a companion and the whistling dark.
crooked_man [angry]: Stop standing in front of each other like that, it spoils the whole joke! Every soul for himself, that is the house rule!
set crooked_man_aversion_known
-> fall_start_menu

~ read_fail
Narrator: You search his twisted face for a seam, but there is only bone, greasepaint, and a grin wide enough to swallow a lantern.
crooked_man [smile]: Go on, stare your fill, I paid dearly for this posture!
-> fall_start_menu

~ laugh_ok
Narrator: Your belly laugh rings out against the rushing wind, and the nightmare hiccups: the plunge slows to a lazy drift while a passing porcelain bathtub blushes pink and hides behind its curtain.
crooked_man [afraid]: Hey now, none of that, this is a tragedy of the highest order! You cannot just chuckle the gravity out of a fellow's drop!
set dream_laughed
-> fall_start_menu

~ laugh_fail
Narrator: The forced laugh catches dry in your throat, swallowed up by the creak of hemp and the roar of falling masonry.
crooked_man [smile]: Oh, a dry house tonight! Do not fret, the drop at the bottom always gets a roar!
-> fall_start_menu

~ fight
crooked_man [sly]: Steel in a falling parlor, how wonderfully rude! Let us see how you dance without a floor!
combat nm_crooked_man

~ after
cutscene nm_noose_runs_out
set crooked_man_fell
if not quest.crooked_nightmare >= dark_wood
quest crooked_nightmare dark_wood
endif
crooked_man [smile]: Curtain call already, and just when we were getting acquainted! Enjoy the lady's little woods, friends, she left the moon on for you!
cutscene nm_noose_runs_out_2
Narrator: His noose jerks taut with a crack, snatching his crooked silhouette up into the dark until you settle, unbruised, into a deep drift of cold autumn leaves.
cutscene end
move nm_dark_wood
